    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is headlined by two high-ceiling anchors: **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.25) and **Corbin Carroll** (67.82). **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a plus-matchup against Jose Soriano, allowing him to capitalize on his power profile from the cleanup spot. Meanwhile, despite a slight platoon dip against a lefty, **Corbin Carroll** remains an essential start. His elite sprint speed and elevated lineup position ensure he stays in the top-tier of our daily output, providing the necessary juice in the scarcest category: Stolen Bases. **Brice Turang** also earns a strong recommendation (61.57), as his placement in the #3 hole against Martin P\u00e9rez creates a high-efficiency environment for both runs and counting stats.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Cole Young**, who just missed the cut at 41.98. While his prospect pedigree and plate discipline are enticing, he was edged out by the superior matchup context afforded to **Kyle Karros** and **Henry Bolte**. Even with **Kyle Karros** facing a potential drag from an elite-armed catcher, the park factors currently favor his setup over the limited ceiling **Cole Young** presents against Jesus Suarez. Elsewhere, we are exercising caution with **Austin Riley** (45.54); facing an arm as sharp as Robert Misiorowski makes his output volatile, but he remains in the lineup due to the lack of viable depth while **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Giancarlo Stanton** remain sidelined on the IL.\n\nManagers should keep a close eye on the Gausman start against **Seiya Suzuki** (52.85). While the park environment is favorable, Gausman\u2019s ability to miss bats presents a risk to our team's batting average floor. However, **Seiya Suzuki** earns a slight bump due to a slower-than-average delivery from the mound, which may provide a narrow window for opportunistic base running\u2014a critical factor for our internal scoring model. All other active roster members, including **Dalton Rushing**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Alex Freeland**, **James Wood**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, **Max Muncy**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Carson Williams**, are cleared for duty, though we will continue to monitor weather reports for late-breaking pivots.",
